================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

None. Shellforge runs on the Python standard library alone.

That is a deliberate constraint rather than an accident: it has to run in the
same CI job as SHELLHOUND's own test suite, which takes no extra dependencies
either. Word material is shipped in `shellforge/corpus.py` instead of pulled
from a generator library, because a tool whose output changes with somebody
else's release cadence is not reproducible, and reproducibility is the whole
premise here.

Scoring a case reads SHELLHOUND (https://github.com/Mateodevv/shellhound,
Apache-2.0) if a checkout is present. It is not vendored, not bundled and not
required to generate a case.

================================================================================
On the contents of generated cases
================================================================================

Everything Shellforge emits is invented.

  * IP addresses come from the documentation ranges reserved by RFC 5737
    (192.0.2.0/24, 198.51.100.0/24, 203.0.113.0/24). No address that routes.
  * Domains end in .test, reserved by RFC 6761.
  * Personal names, plugin names and content are made up. Any resemblance to
    a real plugin is unintended; a real plugin name in a fixture would
    eventually be read as an accusation against that plugin.
  * Password hashes have the SHAPE of a phpass hash and are hashes of
    nothing. There is nothing to crack.
  * Payloads are inert markers in the spirit of an EICAR file: the shortest
    text that carries a pattern a detector looks for, and nothing else. No
    generated file is a working web shell, and none ever should be.

No data from any real incident is contained in this repository or produced by
it.

The user agent strings in `shellforge/corpus.py` are real, because a log whose
agents are invented is not a log a parser can be tested against. They identify
browser and crawler software, not people.
